File System and Storage.

The basic process for adding storage to system is:
- install the drive 
- partition it
- add a filesystem and then mount it

All hardware device are mappeed to the /dev directory. Storage disk are displayed there using the sd string.

## hwinfo command - dispplay detail about system component.
hwinfo --storage = display storage controllers.
hwinfo --block = display in storage disk and partitions.

## lsblk command - display information about the storage device the system is aware of.

## MBR - Master Boot Record
This help to partition the harddrive, we can also use GUID.

## fdisk command help to do partition.Its a menu driven command.

## Parted utility is another good partition management tool in line with fdisk.

### growpart - utility is used to extend the partition

After partition are created they needed to be update.
- partprobe command scan storage disk and partition changes
- Partion information are store in file name /proc/partitions

### blkid - display the UUID of the partitions.

####################################################################################

After creating partition we need to add file systemto organize storage of data.
-There are two type of filesystem in linux mostly used 
1. ext4 
2. XFS

*** ext4 ***
# We use mkfs - make filesystem command to new portion created on disk.
example - mkfs.ext4 /dev/sdb2. or mkfs -t /dev/sdb2

if the portion is not new mkfs overwrite in the portition

### XFS has more advantages over ext4 
1. XFS recognizes a larger partition size
2. XFS recognizes a larger file size.
3. XFS avoids inode exhaustion.


### fsck - to check and repair the file system
_ This only work when the filesystem is unmount 
fsck -y /dev/sdb2 will check and repair the file system.
